# File spec for ./vyniltestset.rs — the TestSet document data contract. Loading,
# merging, templating and assert evaluation belong to ./handler.rs and ./vyniltest.rs.

Spec: VynilTestSet

Platform: Rust

Purpose:
  The declarative serde schema of the `TestSet` document kind plus the shared assert
    vocabulary (@VynilAssert, @VynilAssertSelector, @VynilAssertMatch, @VynilAssertResult)
    and the mock envelope (@VynilTestSetMocks) that @VynilTest reuses: pure data types
    whose only behavioural lever is field requiredness. The file declares no function and
    no impl block — parsing, the TestSet duplicate-name abort, reference validation
    (@TestHandler::validate_refs, defined on @TestHandler in ./handler.rs with no current
    caller) and every match semantic live in the consumer files, so this contract is
    exactly the wire shape a `vinyl.solidite.fr/v1beta1` `TestSet` document and a
    @VynilAssertResult result row must have.

Owns:
  ./vyniltestset.rs

References:
  ./../package/test.sdd — the parse-side freeze this shape must match: non-recursive
    `.yml`/`.yaml` scan, the pre-parse apiVersion gate `vinyl.solidite.fr/v1beta1`
    (literal `vinyl` spelling) and `kind` dispatch, parse failures surfaced as
    @common::Error::YamlError with `{file}: `-prefixed messages, and Test/TestSet
    duplicate-name abort keyed by @VynilTestSetMeta.name.
  ./handler.rs — loader/merger/templater (./handler.sdd pending): deserializes these
    types through @serde_json::from_value, aborts on a duplicate TestSet name reading
    `duplicate TestSet '{name}'`, and owns @TestHandler::validate_refs, which checks each
    loaded Test's `testSets[].testSet` keys against the loaded TestSet map and is never
    called from ./../package/test.rs.
  ./vyniltest.rs — consumer (./vyniltest.sdd pending): @VynilTest imports five of these
    types (@VynilAssert, @VynilAssertMatch, @VynilAssertResult, @VynilAssertSelector,
    @VynilTestSetMocks), owns selector/matcher semantics (@matches_selector,
    @value_verdict, @count_verdict) and builds @VynilAssertResult rows in
    @VynilTest::run_asserts.
  ./result.rs — output-side consumer: embeds @Vec<@VynilAssertResult> in @TestResult and
    renders @name/@description/@passed/@message into the text, json and JUnit outputs.
  ./mod.rs — re-exports @VynilAssertResult alone at module level (the only item of this
    file promoted to `client::testing::*`); the rest are reached under the
    `vyniltestset::` path.

Depends on:
  `serde`/`serde_json` — the derives, and @serde_json::Value as the untyped payload
    holder; the actual deserialization is YAML → @serde_json::Value → struct, both steps
    performed consumer-side.
  /common/src/lib.sdd — `common::httpmock::@HttpMockItem`, the HTTP mock item held in
    @VynilTestSetMocks.http.
  /common/src/rhaihandler.sdd — @Dynamic, the untyped Kubernetes mock object held in
    @VynilTestSetMocks.kubernetes.

Exposes:
  nine `pub` items, no functions; crate-wide reachable as `client::testing::vyniltestset::*`
    because /agent/src/lib.rs declares `pub mod testing`:
  @VynilTestSet — TestSet root with `#[allow(non_snake_case)]` and @Deserialize/@Serialize/
    @Clone/@Debug: @apiVersion (@String), @kind (@String), @metadata (@VynilTestSetMeta),
    @variables (@Option<@VynilTestSetVariablesSet>), @mocks (@Option<@VynilTestSetMocks>),
    @asserts (@Option<Vec<@VynilAssert>>).
  @VynilTestSetMeta — @name (@String), @description (@Option<@String>).
  @VynilTestSetVariablesSet — `pub type` alias of @BTreeMap<@String, @VynilTestSetVariable>
    (variable name → definition).
  @VynilTestSetVariable — @var_type, renamed on the wire to `type` via
    `#[serde(rename = "type")]` (@String), and @default (@Option<@serde_json::Value>).
  @VynilAssertMatch — enum with `#[serde(rename_all = "snake_case")]` and variants
    @Exact(@u64), @AtLeast(@u64), @AtMost(@u64), @All (carries `#[default]`), @Any,
    @None; derives @PartialEq, @Eq and @Default besides @Clone/@Debug/serde.
  @VynilAssertSelector — @kind, @name, @namespace, all @Option<@String>; interpretation
    (match rules, empty-selector-selects-all) is owned by @matches_selector.
  @VynilAssert — @name (@String), @description (@Option<@String>), @selector
    (@VynilAssertSelector, not @Option), @matcher (@VynilAssertMatch, not @Option),
    @value (@Option<@serde_json::Value>).
  @VynilAssertResult — the output row @name (@String), @description (@Option<@String>),
    @passed (@bool), @message (@String); derives @Clone/@Debug and fully qualified
    @serde::Serialize/@serde::Deserialize.
  @VynilTestSetMocks — mock envelope @http (@Option<Vec<@HttpMockItem>>), @kubernetes
    (@Option<Vec<@Dynamic>>); despite the name it is also the shape of @VynilTest.mocks.

Must:
  Freeze wire keys as the declared Rust field names: no struct carries a container
    rename, so `apiVersion` stays camelCase (hence `#[allow(non_snake_case)]`: the only
    rename in any struct here is @var_type → `type`) and all other keys are single
    lowercase words (`kind`, `metadata`, `variables`, `mocks`, `asserts`, `name`,
    `description`, `default`, `selector`, `matcher`, `value`, `http`, `kubernetes`,
    `passed`, `message`).
  Allow unknown fields at every depth: no `#[serde(deny_unknown_fields)]` exists, so an
    unrecognized key in any mapping (root, metadata, variable, selector, mocks, assert,
    result) is silently dropped; unknown enum variants are still rejected (enum tagging,
    not field tolerance).
  Require exactly `apiVersion`, `kind`, `metadata` on the root, `name` inside metadata,
    `name`/`selector`/`matcher` on each assert, `type` on each variable, and
    `name`/`passed`/`message` on @VynilAssertResult; every other key is @Option and
    absent-or-null on the wire. No `#[serde(default)]` attribute exists anywhere in this
    file — optionality is @Option-only.
  Keep @apiVersion, @kind and @var_type unconstrained @String: the apiVersion gate and
    the `Test`/`TestSet` kind dispatch happen pre-parse in the scanner; nothing
    post-parse inspects @kind or @apiVersion again, and @var_type's value is never read
    by any consumer.
  Encode @VynilAssertMatch externally tagged (serde default, no container attribute):
    unit variants as the scalars `all`, `any`, `none`, count variants as single-key maps
    `exact: N`, `at_least: N`, `at_most: N` with N a @u64 integer; a negative,
    fractional or @u64-overflowing N is a parse error, and camelCase spellings such as
    `atLeast` are unknown-variant errors because only snake_case variant names exist.
  Treat absent keys and `null` identically as @Option::None for every @Option field —
    including `asserts: null` vs `asserts: []`, which differ as @Option::None vs
    @Option::Some of an empty vec and keep that difference in the loaded @VynilTestSet.
  Order @variables deterministically: the @BTreeMap alias keeps entries sorted by
    variable name for consumers walking the declarations.
  Carry no logic here: no function, impl block, constructor or validation exists, the
    only `#[default]` (@VynilAssertMatch::@All) can never fire because `matcher` has no
    serde default, and every type is built by struct literal on all-`pub` fields — by
    @serde_json::from_value in ./handler.rs, by hand for the synthetic `execution` and
    `value_script` rows in ./handler.rs, and by @VynilTest::run_asserts in ./vyniltest.rs.

Accepts:
  A @serde_json::Value mapping produced by the scanner from a `TestSet`-kind,
    `vinyl.solidite.fr/v1beta1` YAML document — the type itself re-validates neither gate
    and imposes no syntax on @name (empty and duplicate-looking names parse; dedup is
    the loader's job).
  @VynilAssertResult additionally accepts plain struct-literal construction from the
    synthetic result rows written by @TestHandler::run_test and @TestHandler::run_test_inner.

Returns:
  A fully populated struct on success, all fields readable (every field is `pub`, every
    type @Clone and @Debug).
  On the serialize side @VynilAssertResult is the only type ever actually serialized (by
    ./result.rs): keys `name`, `description` (emitted as null when @Option::None),
    `passed`, `message`; nothing serializes @VynilTestSet, @VynilAssert or @VynilTestSetMocks.

Raises:
  Nothing directly — a data-only file has no error lane. Shape violations surface as
    @serde `missing field`, `invalid type` and unknown-variant errors inside the
    consumer's @serde_json::from_value call and are mapped there to @Error::YamlError
    with the `{file}: ` prefix (./../package/test.sdd).

Handles:
  `selector: {}` present-but-empty — deserializes to an all-@Option::None selector; the
    key itself remains required on every assert.
  `type: ""` or any arbitrary @type text — accepted at parse; no consumer interprets it.
  Duplicate variable keys inside one document's mapping — resolved during JSON
    construction before this type is reached; the alias itself defines no policy.

Tasks:
  [ ] Cover the schema with tests — no #[cfg(test)] module exists in this file and no
      in-tree test deserializes a TestSet; the only nearby @VynilAssertResult constructions
      are the helper fns in ./result.rs's tests. Map each scenario to a same-named test:
      minimal-testset-parses, matcher-wire-forms, unknown-keys-ignored,
      asserts-null-vs-empty-list, count-payload-out-of-uint64, required-keys-enforced.
  [?] `type` is required on the wire yet never read — @build_var_context consults only
      @default. Decide whether to validate it against a declared vocabulary or drop the
      requiredness.
  [?] @VynilAssertMatch derives @Default with `#[default]` @All but no path can apply it
      (`matcher` is required, no @serde(default), no @default() caller). Decide whether
      `matcher` should default to `all` or the marker should be dropped.
  [?] @VynilTestSetMocks is shared with @VynilTest.mocks and @TestHandler::get_templated_test
      rebuilds it; the `TestSet` prefix in the name is misleading. Decide a rename or keep.
  [?] @VynilAssertResult derives @Deserialize although nothing deserializes it (results
      flow one way). Decide whether to keep the round-trip derive.

Done when:
  Each scenario maps to a passing test, the `[?]` decisions above are recorded, and
    `cargo test -p agent`, clippy, `cargo +nightly fmt --check` and `specdd lint` stay green.

Scenario: minimal TestSet parses
  Given a mapping with only `apiVersion`, `kind` and `metadata.name`
  When @serde_json::from_value builds a @VynilTestSet
  Then @variables, @mocks and @asserts are @Option::None, @description is @Option::None
  And @apiVersion/@kind hold whatever strings arrived (a non-`TestSet` @kind parses too)
  No mapped test exists.

Scenario: matcher keeps its wire forms
  Given `matcher` given as scalar `all`, `any`, `none`
  When a @VynilAssert deserializes
  Then the variant is @All, @Any, @None and a bare-count lane reads it later
  And Given `exact: 2`, `at_least: 2` or `at_most: 2`
  Then the variant is @Exact(2), @AtLeast(2), @AtMost(2)
  And Given `atLeast: 2` or a missing `matcher` key
  Then deserialization errors (unknown variant / missing field)
  No mapped test exists.

Scenario: unknown keys pass silently
  Given a TestSet root carrying an extra `foo: 1` and an assert carrying an unknown
    `operator` key
  When the documents deserialize
  Then both succeed with the unknown keys dropped and nothing warns
  No mapped test exists.

Scenario: asserts null differs from asserts empty
  Given two TestSet documents, one with `asserts: null`, one with `asserts: []`
  When each @VynilTestSet loads into the handler map
  Then the first holds @Option::None and the second @Option::Some of an empty vec; the
    @Option::Some/None split is what ./handler.rs templates over
  No mapped test exists.

Scenario: count payload bounds reject bad matcher counts
  Given `exact: -1`, `exact: 2.5` or `exact: 18446744073709551616`
  When the assert deserializes
  Then the @u64 payload fails and the document aborts the load as a consumer-side
    `{file}: `-prefixed @Error::YamlError
  No mapped test exists.
